<Layout title="Privacy Policy - Hocking Luxury Lodges" description="Privacy policy for the BOWSWC QuickBooks Online integration." noindex={true}>
  <div class="container py-4">
    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p><strong>Software:</strong> BOWSWC<br />
    <strong>Operator:</strong> Because Our Wives Said We Could LLC ("we", "us")<br />
    <strong>Last updated:</strong> September 1, 2026</p>

    <h2>1. Scope</h2>
    <p>This policy describes how BOWSWC ("the Software") handles data
    obtained through the QuickBooks Online API.</p>
    <p>The Software is a private, internal accounting tool operated by
    Because Our Wives Said We Could LLC for its own business records. It has no customers and no
    public users. It collects no information from visitors to this page.</p>

    <h2>2. What data the Software accesses</h2>
    <p>The Software connects to a single QuickBooks Online company owned by
    Because Our Wives Said We Could LLC. Within that company, it may access:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Financial transactions, including invoices, expenses, bills, and deposits</li>
      <li>Chart of accounts, classes, and other accounting structures</li>
      <li>Customer and vendor records, including names and contact details stored in
        QuickBooks by us</li>
      <li>Standard financial reports, such as profit and loss and balance sheet</li>
    </ul>
    <p>It accesses only the QuickBooks company that authorized it. It does not access
    any other Intuit account, and it cannot access data belonging to any other
    business or individual.</p>

    <h2>3. What the Software writes</h2>
    <p>The Software is capable of recording and modifying accounting transactions in
    the connected QuickBooks company, including creating expenses, allocating
    amounts across accounting classes, and creating supporting records such as
    vendors and classes.</p>
    <p>All such changes occur only within Because Our Wives Said We Could LLC's own QuickBooks company
    and only at our direction.</p>

    <h2>4. How data is stored</h2>
    <p>Data retrieved from QuickBooks is processed on infrastructure controlled by
    Because Our Wives Said We Could LLC. It is not uploaded to any third-party service, not stored
    in any cloud database operated by us, and not transmitted anywhere other than
    between our own systems and Intuit's API.</p>
    <p>OAuth access and refresh tokens are stored on our own systems in files
    restricted to the operating system account running the Software.</p>

    <h2>5. Data sharing</h2>
    <p><strong>We do not sell, rent, share, or transfer QuickBooks data to any third party.</strong></p>
    <p>There is no advertising, no analytics, no tracking, and no data brokerage
    associated with the Software. Data may be disclosed only where required by law,
    or to our own accountant or tax preparer in the ordinary course of preparing our
    financial statements and filings.</p>

    <h2>6. Data retention</h2>
    <p>Locally stored accounting data is retained only as long as needed for our
    bookkeeping and recordkeeping obligations, and may be deleted at any time
    without affecting the records held in QuickBooks Online.</p>
    <p>Authorization tokens are deleted when the connection is revoked.</p>

    <h2>7. Security</h2>
    <p>Access to the Software and its stored credentials is limited to authorized
    representatives of Because Our Wives Said We Could LLC. Credentials are stored with
    filesystem-level access restrictions and are excluded from source control.
    Connections to Intuit are made over HTTPS using Intuit's official OAuth 2.0
    implementation.</p>
    <p>No system is perfectly secure, and we make no guarantee of absolute security.</p>

    <h2>8. Revoking access</h2>
    <p>Authorization can be revoked at any time from within QuickBooks Online, under
    the connected apps settings, or through the Intuit developer console. Revocation
    immediately ends the Software's ability to read or write data.</p>

    <h2>9. Children's privacy</h2>
    <p>The Software is a business accounting tool. It is not directed at children and
    does not knowingly process any personal information relating to children.</p>

    <h2>10. Relationship to Intuit</h2>
    <p>The Software is not produced, endorsed, or supported by Intuit Inc. Data held
    within QuickBooks Online is additionally governed by Intuit's own privacy
    policy, which is not modified by this document.</p>

    <h2>11. Changes</h2>
    <p>This policy may be updated to reflect changes in the Software's behavior. The
    "last updated" date above indicates the most recent revision.</p>

    <h2>12. Contact</h2>
    <p>Questions regarding this policy may be sent to:</p>
    <p><strong>luxehauslodge@gmail.com</strong></p>
  </div>
</Layout>
